From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:44:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Reason: GFSetArray passes the array's pointer to GX

GFSetArray wrote the array base as a physical address (OSCachedToPhysical);
on PC arrays can be the game code's own data (the grass's vertex arrays
are embedded assets), outside the emulated memory a physical address
reaches, so the grass's first draw read from a wrong address. On PC it
calls GXSetArray with the pointer.
---
 src/dolphin/gf/GFGeometry.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/dolphin/gf/GFGeometry.cpp b/src/dolphin/gf/GFGeometry.cpp
index 77c2a6da..7e43ddcf 100644
--- a/src/dolphin/gf/GFGeometry.cpp
+++ b/src/dolphin/gf/GFGeometry.cpp
@@ -235,6 +235,13 @@ void GFSetVtxAttrFmtv(GXVtxFmt vtxfmt, GXVtxAttrFmtList* list) {
 }
 
 void GFSetArray(GXAttr attr, void* base_ptr, u8 stride) {
+#ifdef TARGET_PC
+    // tww-vita: arrays can be the game code's own data (the grass's), outside
+    // the emulated GameCube memory a physical address can name; the GX call
+    // takes the pointer itself.
+    GXSetArray(attr, base_ptr, stride);
+    return;
+#endif
     s32 cpAttr;
     if (attr == GX_VA_NBT) {
         cpAttr = GX_VA_TEX0MTXIDX;
-- 
